Z||000000||Kerry Lacy||08-17-2001||03:03 PM||||My temp gage will slightly move but not even to the 100 degree mark.  I have a low temp fan switch and 160 degree termostat with the hypertech chip.  The 86SE 2.8 has been showing the correct temp up untill a few days ago.  now it will not even register 100degrees.  replaced the connector and grounded it. The gage pegs hot when grounded and the hot light will come on.  Replaced the switch /sensor snd still no temp.  Checked the switch /sensor to make sure it was grounded and it is.  Took the dash out to see if the needle had fallen off and it is where it is supposed to be.  Could it be the termostst? Someone told me it may be stuck open, but after a while at idle the cooling fan comes on.  I think it is the gage but for $100.00 I thought I would see if anyone had a different idea.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||08-17-2001||03:13 PM||||Sounds like the gauge to me but no need to pay $100 bucks for one when you can buy full gauges sets for $20 or less all over the place.<P>Someone else may know how to test to make sure it is the gauge.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
